      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-guts-2019-pm-13.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "25\nWe know \\(A \\cdot \\overline{A B}\\) ends in 0 . Since neither is 0 , they must be 2,5 in some order. We easily find that \\(A=2, B=5\\) works while the opposite doesn't, so \\(\\overline{A B}=25\\).",
